      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the length of the longest side of a similar triangle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the perimeter of the original triangle:**\n   The sides of the original triangle are 6 cm, 7 cm, and 9 cm. Therefore, the perimeter \\( P \\) is:\n   \\[\n   P = 6 + 7 + 9 = 22 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the scale factor:**\n   The perimeter of the similar triangle is given as 110 cm. The scale factor \\( k \\) is the ratio of the perimeter of the similar triangle to the perimeter of the original triangle:\n   \\[\n   k = \\frac{110}{22} = 5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the length of the longest side of the similar triangle:**\n   The longest side of the original triangle is 9 cm. The length of the longest side \\( L \\) of the similar triangle is:\n   \\[\n   L = 9 \\times k = 9 \\times 5 = 45 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the longest side of the similar triangle is \\(\\boxed{45}\\).",
